hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8581","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, he said: Anas said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with one of his mothers. believers, so she sent another bowl with food in it. It struck the Messenger’s hand, and the bowl fell and broke, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it. He handed over the two pieces of food to him, joined one to the other, and began to gather food into them, saying: “Your mother has become jealous, eat.” So they ate. So he ordered that she bring the bowl she had in her house, so he gave the correct bowl to the Messenger, and left the broken bowl in the house of the one who had broken it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8582","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Asad bin Musa, he said: we are Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Umm Salamah, It means that she brought food in a bowl of hers to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions. Then Aisha came, wrapped in a cloak, and with her. Then she tore the plate with it, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, joined the two parts of the plate and said: “Eat, your mother has become jealous” twice, then The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took Aisha’s scroll, sent it to Umm Salamah, and gave Umm Salamah’s scroll to Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8583","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Falayt, on the authority of Jasra bint Dajaja, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I have never seen a food maker like Safia! She gave the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, a vessel containing food, but I could not bring myself to break it, so I asked the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, about His atonement, and he said: “A vessel like a vessel, and food like food.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8584","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani told us, he said: Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ claimed that he heard Ubaid bin Umair saying: I heard Aisha claims that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stay with Zainab bint Jahsh and drink honey with her, so I made peace with her. And Hafsa, that any of us, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her, let her say: I smell the scent of maghafir from you. She ate maghafir, so he entered upon me. One of them said that to him, and he said: “No, but I drank honey with Zainab bint Jahsh, and I will not go back to it.” So she revealed: O Prophet, why You prohibit what God has made lawful for you, seeking the pleasure of your wives, if you repent to God, for Aisha and Hafsa, and when the Prophet confided to some recently married him, because he said: “Rather, I drank honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8585","Ibrahim bin Yunus bin Muhammad Harami told us, he said: my father told us, he said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, “He had a female slave whom he could roam, but Aisha and Hafsa did not cease to be with him until he made them forbidden to himself.” So God revealed God Almighty: O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you, until the end of the verse? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8586","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah bin Al-Samit, that Aisha, She said: I sought the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I put my hand in his hair, and he said: “Your devil has come to you,” so I said: Do you not have a devil? He said: “Yes, but God helped me with it, so he became Muslim.”"
"8587","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I lost the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I thought that he had gone to see some of his wives, so I felt him, and behold, he was kneeling, or prostrating, saying: “Glory be to You and praise be to You, there is no god but You.” She said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, you are in a matter, and I am in a matter. Another"
"8588","Ishaq bin Mansour told me, he said: I am Abd al-Razzaq, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika informed me, that Aisha, she said: I missed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, and I thought that he had gone to some of his wives, so I felt him, then I came back, and lo and behold, he was kneeling or prostrating, saying: “Glory be to You and with Your praise, there is no god but You.” So I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. One matter, but I am in another (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8589","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Kathir, that he heard Muhammad bin Qays, saying: I heard Aisha, saying: Shall I not tell you about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and about me? We said: Yes, she said: When it was my night, he turned over, put his sandals on his feet, put on his cloak, and spread the edge of his garment over He went to his bed, and he only stayed until he thought that I had fallen asleep. Then he slowly put on his shoes, and slowly took his robe, then he slowly opened the door. So he came out and went to him slowly, and I put my shield over my head, and covered myself, and covered myself with my garment, and set off in pursuit of him, until Al-Baqi’ came, and he raised He raised his hands three times, and he prolonged standing, then he deviated and I deviated, so he hurried, and I hurried, and he hurried, and I hurried, and he came and I came, I overtook him, so I entered, and it was not until I lay down that he entered and said: “What is the matter with you, O Aish, Rabiyya?” Suleiman said: “I thought it was good.” He said: “ Hashia.” I said: Nothing. He said: “You will tell me, or the gentle and knowledgeable one will tell me.” I said: O Messenger of God, so I told him the news. He said: “ Are you the blackness that I saw in front of me? I said: Yes. She said: He gave me a sore in my chest that hurt me. He said: Did you think that God would be unjust to you? And His Messenger.” She said: “Whatever people conceal, God knows.” He said: “Yes, for Gabriel came to me when I saw you, and he did not enter upon you. And you had put on your clothes, and he called me and hid it from you, and I answered him, but I hid it from you, and I thought that you had fallen asleep, but I hated to I wake you up, and I was afraid that you would feel lonely, so he ordered me to go to the people of Al-Baqi’ and ask forgiveness for them.” Hajjaj disagreed with him and said: On the authority of Ibn Jurayj, On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8590","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Mulaika told me, He heard Muhammad bin Qais bin Makhramah say: I heard Aisha speaking. She said: Shall I not tell you about me and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? And peace be upon him? We said: Yes. She said: When it was the night that he was with me, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he turned over and placed his sandals on his feet. He put on his robe and spread the edge of his garment on his bed. He only stayed there until he thought that I had fallen asleep. Then he slowly put on his shoes and took He slowly took off his cloak, then he slowly opened the door, and he came out and dried it slowly, and I put my shield on my head, and covered myself, and covered myself with my cloak. I set off in pursuit of him, and he came to Al-Baqi’, and he raised his hands three times and continued standing for a long time, then he turned away, and I turned away, so he sped up, and I sped up. He ran, and I ran, so he brought, so I brought, and I outpaced him, so I went in. It was not until I lay down that he came in and said: “What do you have, O Aish, with a blanket?” “Rabiyya?” She said: No. He said: “You will inform me, or the gentle and knowledgeable one will inform me.” I said: O Messenger of God, may my mother and father be sacrificed for you. So I told him the news. He said: “Are you the blackness that I saw in front of me?” She said: “Yes.” He gave me a moment to calm my chest that hurt me, then he said: “ Did you think that God and His Messenger would be unjust to you?” She said: “Whatever people conceal, God knows it.” He said: “Yes, for Gabriel came to me when he came to me.” I saw, but he was not entering upon you, while you had put on your clothes, so he called me and was hidden from you, so I answered him, but I was hidden from you, and I thought that I had You lay down, and I was afraid that you would feel lonely, so he ordered me to go to the people of Al-Baqi’ and ask forgiveness for them.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad In Ibn Juraij, it is more proven in our view than Ibn Wahb. It was narrated by Asim on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of other than this. Pronunciation (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8591","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, on the authority of Asim bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Aisha She said: I lost him during the night, so I followed him, and behold, he was in Al-Baqi’. He said: “Peace be upon you, the abode of a believing people. You are our great companion. And we will catch up. Oh God, do not deprive us of their reward, and do not test us after them.” She said: Then he turned to me and said: “Woe to her, if you could, you would not \She did\"""""
"8592","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Humaid told us, and he is the son of Abd al-Rahman al-Rawasi, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha said: “I have never been more jealous of a woman than I am of Khadija because of the frequent mention of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to her.” She said: He married me three years later.”"
"8593","Abdah bin Abdullah Al-Saffar Al-Basri told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Bishr, he said: Zakaria told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Bahi, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I did not know until Zainab entered upon me without permission while I was angry, then she said to the Messenger of God: It will suffice for you if Abu Bakr’s daughter turns her two daughters to you, then comes to me and you turn away from her, until the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: So I approached her until I saw that her saliva had dried up in her mouth, not responding to me at all. Then I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. His face lights up (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8594","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, he said: My father told me, On the authority of Khaled bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Bahi, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I did not know until I entered upon Zainab without permission, and she He became angry, then she said: It will suffice for you if Abu Bakr’s daughter turns two of her offspring for you, then she comes to me, so I turn away from her, so the Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Become victorious.” So I approached her until I saw that her saliva had dried up in her mouth. She did not respond to me at all, so I saw The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a cheerful face. Ishaq ibn Yusuf disagreed with him. Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim told me, he said: Ishaq told us On the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Khalid bin Salamah, on the authority of Al-Bahi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I did not know until Zainab entered without permission, and she He became angry,” and he mentioned something similar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8595","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Aisha said: Sawda visited us one day, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat between me and her, one of his legs on my lap, and the other on her lap. So I made her a harira, or he said: a harira, so I said: Eat, but she refused, so I said: So that you may eat, or that I may smear your face, but she refused, so I took She took something from the piece, so I smeared it on her face, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his foot from her lap, so she could take some of it from me, so she took I took something from the piece, so I smeared it on my face, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was laughing, then I saw Umar, saying: O Abdullah bin Omar, oh Abdullah bin Omar, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Get up and wash your faces, for I do not think Omar is anything but an insider.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8596","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Al-Mala’i, meaning Abu Nu’aym Al-Fadl bin Dakin, he said: Isa bin Tahman, he said: I heard Anas He says: Zainab used to boast about the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, God granted me marriage from heaven, and in it the verse about the veil was revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8597","Abu Asim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: It has reached Safiya that Hafsa, she said: daughter A Jew, so she cried, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her while she was crying, and said: “What makes you cry?” She said: Hafsa said to me: Daughter. A Jew, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You are the daughter of a prophet, and your uncle is a prophet, and you are under a prophet, so what are you proud of?” Then he said: “Fear God, O Hafsa.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8598","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq, he said: Abdul Razzaq, he said: Muammar, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have a husband, and I have a wife. Should I say he gave me such-and-such, and clothed me with such-and-such, and this is a lie? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is saturated with what he was not given is like one who wears two false garments.”"
"8599","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, he said: Fatima told me, on the authority of Asma, that a woman, She said: O Messenger of God, I have a wife, so is there any blame on me if I am satisfied with my husband with anything other than what he gives me? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who is saturated with what he was not given is like one who wears two false garments.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is the truth and the one who There was an error before him. Muhammad ibn Adam told us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa, who said: “The Prophet’s wife came May God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” and he mentioned something similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8600","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Urwa told him, Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives and see which of them had her share come out.” He took her out with him, and he used to allocate to each woman her day and night, except that Sawda bint Zam’ah gave her day And her night is for Aisha, seeking thereby the satisfaction of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8601","Yusuf bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ataa told me, he said: We attended with Ibn Abbas Maymunah’s funeral. The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was extravagant. Ibn Abbas said: “This is the wife of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So if you raise Its coffin, do not disturb it, do not shake it, and be gentle, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had nine, and he used to divide for eight, and does not divide by one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8602","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir told me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he married her, and Jacob said: When He married Umm Salamah, stayed with her for three days, and said to her: “You are not to be disgraced by your family. If you wish, I will do the same for you, and if I do the same for you, “I have sworn to my wives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8603","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Qattan al-Ruqqi told me, he said: Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Habib bin Abi Thabit told me that Abd Al-Hamid bin Abdullah bin Abi Amr and Al-Qasim bin Muhammad told him that they heard Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith, It is reported that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him, saying: When Zainab gave birth, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me. So he proposed to me, and I said: You are not married like me. As for me, I have no children, and I am jealous and have children. He said: “I am older than you. As for jealousy... Then God will take her away, and as for the children, they will go to God and His Messenger.” So he married her, and he began to go to her and say: “Where is Zanab?” until Ammar came One day, he stroked her and said: This woman is breastfeeding the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was breastfeeding her. He came to me and said: “Where is Zinab?” A relative, she said, and he agreed with her then: Ammar took her, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I will come to you tonight,” so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, spent the night. And peace be upon him. Then in the morning, he said: When the morning came: “You are an honor upon your family, so if you wish, I can do seven for you, and if I do seven, I will do seven for my wives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8604","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I was jealous of those who gave themselves to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said, ‘Can a woman give herself to a man?! Then God Almighty revealed: You may put to yourself whomsoever you wish of them and give shelter to yourself whomsoever you wish and whomsoever you desire of those whom you have set aside - there is no blame on you. I said: “By God, I do not see your Lord but that He hastens for you in your desires.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8605","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad Al-Muaddeb told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Sharik, “She was among those who gave herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8606","Muhammad ibn Adam informed me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “If he wants to travel, he casts lots among his wives, whichever of them his arrow produces, he takes it out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8607","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: I am Al-Shafi’i, he said: Muhammad bin Ali bin Shafi’i informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives, and whichever of them produced an arrow, he would take it out.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8608","Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani informed us, he said: Ya'qub, that is Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, informed us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas, and 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah related to me, from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him, when the people of the slander (ahl al-ifk) said what they said about her, and Allah exonerated her. He said: Each of them related to me a portion of her hadith, and some of them were more retentive of her hadith than others, and more precise in its transmission. I have preserved from each of them the hadith that he related to me from 'A'ishah, and some of their hadith corroborates some, even though some were more retentive than others. They said: 'A'ishah said: When the Prophet, peace be upon him, intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives, and whichever of them had her lot drawn, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, would take her with him. 'A'ishah said: So he drew lots among us in a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, after the command of the hijab had been revealed. I was carried in a hawdaj (litter) and placed in it. We traveled until the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, had finished that expedition and was returning, and we were approaching Madinah on the return journey. He announced the departure one night, so I rose when they announced the departure, and I walked until I had passed the army. When I had taken care of my need, I returned to my camp, and I felt for my chest, and lo, there was a necklace of mine made from Zafar beads, broken. I went back searching for my necklace, and my search for it detained me. The party who used to prepare my hawdaj came, and they lifted my hawdaj and placed it on the camel I used to ride, thinking that I was in it. At that time, women were light; they were not heavy with flesh, nor did meat cover them—they merely ate a morsel of food. So the people did not find the hawdaj light when they raised it and carried it, and I was a young girl. They sent the camel forth and departed. I found my necklace after the army had moved on, and I came to their encampment, but there was not a single person among them calling or responding. I took my place where I had been, thinking they would miss me and return to me. While I was sitting in my place, sleep overcame me, and I slept. Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal al-Sulami, then al-Dhakwani, was behind the army. He came to my place at dawn and saw the dark form of a person. He recognized me when he saw me, for he had seen me before the hijab. I awoke at his exclamation when he recognized me, and I covered my face with my jilbab. By Allah, we did not speak a single word, nor did I hear from him a single word except his exclamation. He knelt down and made his she-camel kneel, and I rose to her and mounted her. He set forth, leading the she-camel, until we reached the army when they were dismounting at midday. Perished those who perished. And the one who took the leading part in the slander was 'Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul. 'Urwah said: 'A'ishah used to dislike that Hassan be reviled in her presence, and she would say: Indeed, he has said: \For my father"," my ancestor"," and my honour are the shield of the honour of Muhammad against you.\"" 'A'ishah said: We arrived in Madinah"," and when we arrived I fell ill for a month"," while the people were spreading the words of the people of the slander. I was unaware of any of that"," and what made me suspicious in my ailment was that I did not recognize from the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," the tenderness I used to see from him when I fell ill. The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," would enter upon me and then say: \""How are you?\"" and then he would leave. That made me suspicious"," though I sensed no harm. Until I went out when I had recovered"," and Umm Mistah went out with me to the open spaces (al-manasik). She used to be our place of relief"," and we used not to go out except from night to night"," before the privies were taken close to our houses. Our affair was that of the early Arabs"," and we used to dislike taking privies near our houses. So I and Umm Mistah set out toward our house when we had finished our business. Umm Mistah stumbled on her garment and said: \""Woe to Mistah!\"" I said to her: \""Shame on what you have said! Do you revile a man who witnessed Badr?\"" She said: \""O you there"," have you not heard what he said?\"" I said: \""And what did he say?\"" She informed me of the words of the people of the slander"," and I became sicker on top of my sickness. When I returned to my house"," the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," entered upon me and then said: \""How are you?\"" I said to him: \""Permit me to go to my parents"," for I wish to verify the news from them.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," gave me permission. I came to my parents and said to my mother: \""O my mother"," what are the people talking about?\"" She said: \""O my daughter"," be easy upon yourself. For rarely has there ever been a beautiful woman with a man who loves her and who has co-wives"," except that they would increase in slandering her.\"" I said: \""Glory to Allah! Have the people really talked about this?\"" I wept that night until morning"," with my tears not ceasing and my eyes not finding sleep. Then I woke weeping in the morning. The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," called 'Ali ibn Abi Talib and Usamah ibn Zayd when the revelation was delayed"," seeking their counsel regarding separation from his family. As for Usamah"," he indicated to the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," what he knew of the innocence of his family and what he knew of goodness in himself. Usamah said: \""Your family"," and we know nothing but good.\"" As for 'Ali"," he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Allah has not constrained you"," and there are many other women besides her. Ask the slave girl"," and she will tell you truly.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," called Barirah and said: \""O Barirah"," have you seen anything that arouses your suspicion?\"" She said: \""By the One who sent you with the truth"," I have never seen anything concerning her that I would fault"," except that she is a young girl who sleeps and leaves the dough of her family"," and the domestic fowl comes and eats it.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," rose that day and sought to excuse himself from 'Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul while he was upon the minbar. He said: \""O company of Muslims"," who will excuse me regarding a man whose harm has reached my family? By Allah"," I know nothing concerning my family but good"," and they have mentioned a man about whom I know nothing but good"," and he does not enter upon my family except with me.\"" Sa'd ibn Mu'adh"," the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Ash'hal"," rose and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I will excuse you from him. If he is from the Aws"," I will strike his neck"," and if he is from our brothers"," the Khazraj"," command us"," and we will carry out your command.\"" She said: A man from the Khazraj rose"," and the mother of Hassan was his cousin from his clan"," and that was Sa'd ibn 'Ubada"," the chief of the Khazraj. She said: Before that he had been a righteous man"," but tribal zeal overcame him. He said to Sa'd ibn Mu'adh: \""You have lied"," by the might of Allah! You will not kill him"," and you have no power to kill him.\"" Usayd ibn Hudayr rose"," and he was the paternal uncle of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. He said to Sa'd ibn 'Ubada: \""You have lied"," by the might of Allah! He will indeed kill him"," for you are a hypocrite"," arguing on behalf of the hypocrites.\"" The two tribes"," the Aws and the Khazraj"," rose up"," almost coming to fight"," while the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," was standing upon the minbar. He kept calming them until they fell silent"," and he fell silent. She said: I wept that day"," my tears did not cease"," and I found no sleep. My parents came to me"," having remained for two nights and a day without sleep"," until I thought my weeping would split my liver. While my parents were sitting with me and I was weeping"," a woman from the Ansar sought permission to enter"," and I gave her permission"," and she began to weep with me. While we were in that state"," the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," entered"," offered salam"," and then sat down. He had not sat with me since the matter was mentioned before that. A month had passed without anything being revealed to him concerning my affair. The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," pronounced the tashahhud when he sat"," and then said: \""To proceed"," O 'A'ishah"," indeed such-and-such has reached me concerning you. If you are innocent"," then Allah will exonerate you"," and if you have committed any sin"," then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him"," for when a servant confesses a sin and then repents"," Allah accepts his repentance.\"" When the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," had finished his words"," my tears dried up until I could not perceive a single drop. I said to my father: \""Answer the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," regarding what he said.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him.\"" I said to my mother: \""Answer the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," regarding what he said.\"" She said: \""By Allah"," I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him.\"" I said"," and I was a young girl who did not read much of the Qur'an: \""By Allah"," I have known—you have heard this hadith until it settled in your souls and you believed it. If I say to you that I am innocent"," you will not believe me"," and if I confess to you a matter"," and Allah knows that I am innocent of it"," you will believe me. By Allah"," I find no example for myself or for you except the father of Yusuf"," when he said: 'So patience is most beautiful"," and Allah is the One sought for help against what you describe.'\"" Then I turned over and lay upon my bed"," and Allah knew at that moment that I was innocent and that Allah would exonerate me of my innocence. But"," by Allah"," I did not think that Allah would send down concerning my affair a revelation that would be recited. My affair"," in my own estimation"," was too insignificant for Allah to speak concerning me with a matter. But I hoped that the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," would see in a dream a vision by which Allah would exonerate me. She said: By Allah"," the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," did not leave his seat"," nor did anyone of the household leave"," until the revelation came down upon him. There overtook him what used to overtake him of the buraha (the heavy distress of revelation)"," until the sweat would drip from him like pearls"," on a cold day"," from the weight of the revelation that was sent down upon him. He said: The relief came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," and he was laughing. The first word he spoke was: \""O 'A'ishah"," as for Allah"," He has exonerated you.\"" My mother said to me: \""Rise to him.\"" I said: \""By Allah"," I will not rise to him"," and I praise none but Allah.\"" She said: And Allah sent down: \""Indeed"," those who brought the slander are a band of you. Do not think it evil for you; rather"," it is good for you. For every man among them is what he has earned of the sin\""—all ten verses. When Allah sent down this concerning my innocence"," Abu Bakr al-Siddiq"," who used to spend on Mistah due to his kinship and his poverty"," said: \""By Allah"," I will never spend anything on Mistah ever"," after what he said about 'A'ishah.\"" So Allah"," the Most High"," sent down: \""And let not those of virtue and wealth among you swear against giving to the near relatives"," the poor"," and the emigrants in the cause of Allah. Let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving"," Merciful.\"" Abu Bakr said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," I love that Allah should forgive me.\"" So he returned to Mistah"," upon whom he used to spend"," and said: \""By Allah"," I will never withhold it from him ever.\"" 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah"," peace be upon him"," asked Zaynab bint Jahsh about my affair. He said to Zaynab: \""What have you known"," or what have you seen?\"" 'A'ishah said: She was the one who used to rival me among the wives of the Prophet"," peace be upon him"," but Allah protected her through her scrupulousness (wara'). Her sister Hamnah fought on her behalf"," and she perished among those who perished. Ibn Shihab said: This is what has reached me from the hadith of this group."""
"8609","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, he said: Abdul-Wahid bin Ayman told us, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, On the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he went out, he would cast lots among his wives, and they would fly.” The lottery was for Aisha and Hafsa, so they all went out with him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to walk with him at night. Aisha, and he was talking to her. Then Hafsa said to Aisha: Will you not ride with my camel tonight, and I will ride with yours, and you will wait and I will wait? She said: Yes, so Aisha rode on Hafsa’s camel, and Hafsa rode on Aisha’s camel, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He went to Aisha's camel, with Hafsa on it, so he greeted her, then walked with her, until they disembarked, and Aisha missed him, so she became jealous, so when she dismounted She began to place her feet between the palms and say: O Lord, send down upon me a scorpion or a snake that will sting me, on the authority of Your Messenger, may God bless him. He said hello, but I cannot say anything to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8610","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Aisha, She said: He found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with Safiyya, and she said to me: Is it yours until you please the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on my behalf? And I make my day for you? I said: Yes, so I took a veil for her dyed with saffron, sprinkled it with water, then covered my veil with it, and I went in on it on her day, so I sat. To his side, and he said: “To you, Aisha, this is not your day.” So I said: God gives it to whomever He wishes, and then I told him My news (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8611","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I have never seen a woman in Her slaughterhouse was like that of Sawda bint Zam’ah, from a woman who was sharp. When she grew up, she said: O Messenger of God, I have made my day because of you. For Aisha, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “allocated two days for Aisha: her day, and the day of Sawdah.”"
"8612","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told me, he said: I asked Aisha, Regarding the illness of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “He complained, and he stopped breathing, and we likened his breathing to that of a raisin eater, and he was He went around to visit his wives, and when the illness became severe, he asked them for permission to nurse with me and for them to visit him, so I granted him permission, so he entered upon me, and he was leaning on Two men, whose feet trace the earth in a line. One of them is Al-Abbas. So I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: Didn’t she tell you who the other one was? I said: No, he said: He is Ali (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8613","Muhammad bin Amir told me, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told me, he said: Abbad bin Abbad told me, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Muadhah, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to “ask us for permission on the Day of Uhud” after it was revealed: “You may put off whomever you wish of them, and you may take to yourself whomever you wish.” She wants, and Mu'adh said: So I said: What did you say to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he asked your permission? She said: I used to say: If that were up to me, I would not prefer anyone over myself. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8614","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I got married, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Did you get married, Jabir?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “A virgin or a married woman?” I said: “No, but a married man.” He said: “Would you not play with her and play with you, a virgin?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8615","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Saeed bin Hafs told us, he said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Yazid Abi Abd al-Rahim, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said: I saw Jabir bin Abdullah and Jabir bin Umair Al-Ansari shooting, he said: As for One of them sat down, and his friend said to him: Are you lazy? He said: Yes, so one of them said to the other: Did you not hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Everything that is not from the remembrance of God is a game, no.” “There will be four things: a man playing with his wife, a man training his horse, a man walking between two places, and a man learning to swim.”"
"8616","Muhammad ibn Wahb al-Harrani informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahim, he said: Abd al-Rahim al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah said: I saw Jabir bin Abdullah and Jabir bin Umair, two Ansari shooting, so one of them said to his friend: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Everything that does not involve the remembrance of God is amusement and play, except for four: a man playing with his wife.” “And a man training his horse, and his walking between the two ends, and teaching a man to swim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8617","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab bin Bakht, On the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said: I saw Jabir bin Abdullah and Jabir bin Umair the Ansari shooting, so one of them turned away and sat down. The other said: Are you lazy? I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Everything that is not from the remembrance of God is idle talk and distraction, except for four characteristics: walking between the two purposes, and his training his horse, and playing with his family, and teaching him to swim.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8618","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Abu Nadra told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said We were walking with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said to me: “Have you married after your father?” I said: Yes. He said: “Are you married or a virgin?” I said. He said: “Will you not marry a virgin, so that she can make you laugh and you can make her laugh, and she can play with you and you play with her?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8619","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raced against me, and I outpaced him. Even when we were exhausted by the meat, he raced against me and he outran me, and said: “This is your house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8620","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwa, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman On the authority of Aisha, she said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was lean on meat, so we camped at a house, and he said to his companions: “Come forward.” Then he said to me: “Come so that I may race against you.” So he raced against me, so I raced against him. Then I went out with him on another journey, and I carried the meat, so we went down to a certain place. So he said to his companions: “Come ahead.” Then he said to me: “Come, I will race with you.” So he raced against me, and he raced past me. He struck me on the shoulder with his hand and said: “This one with that one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8621","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told me, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told me, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were on a journey, and his companions came forward, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be ahead of me.” She said: So I raced to him, so I raced to him, and when it was later, and I carried the meat, he said: “Race me.” So I raced to him, and he raced to me, and he said: “This is the one with that.” \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8622","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali Al-Masisi told me, he said: Saeed bin Al-Mughirah Abu Uthman Al-Sayyad told me, in the book of biographies, he said: Al-Fazari told me, On the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Aisha told me that she was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, was on a journey while she was a slave girl, so he said to his companions: “Come forward,” then he said: “Come, I will race with you.” So I raced to him, and I raced to him on my two feet. When he was still gone, I went out with him on a journey, and he said to his companions: “Come forward.” Then he said: “Come, I will go ahead of you.” And I forgot what was going on, and I had carried the meat. So I said: How can I race against you, O Messenger of God, when I am in this condition? He said: “You will do it.” So I raced to him, and he raced to me, and he said: “This is with that precedence.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8623","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ali, meaning Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I was I play with the girls in the house of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I have companions who come to me and they play with me, so they hide when they see the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would sneak them to me, and they would play with me.”"
"8624","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Ja`far ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha She said: I was playing with the girls, and perhaps the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my companions entered my house. When they saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I and my companions were with me. May God bless him and grant him peace. They fled, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As you are and as you are.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8625","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Hujayn narrated to us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is Ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to sneak to me my companions who would play with me with toys: little girls.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8626","Ibrahim bin Saeed Al-Jawhari told us, he said: Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Wahib bin Khalid, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I used to play with girls during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"8627","Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Amara bin Ghaziyah told me, that Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Al-Harith narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from A raid, and I placed a cloak on the door of my room, and an Armenian curtain on the width of her house. He entered the house, and when he saw it, he said to me: “O Aisha, “My money is for the world.” Then the bread was torn apart, until it touched the ground, and in its plain was a covering. Then a wind blew, revealing the daughters of Aisha. He was playing, so he said: “What is this, Aisha?” She said: My daughters, and he saw between their backs a horse with two wings. He said: “And what is this that I see?” Their middle? She said: A horse. He said: What is that on it? She said: Two wings. He said: A horse with two wings? I heard that Solomon had horses with wings, so he, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed until I saw their molars. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8628","I am Yunus bin Abdul-Ala. He said: I am Ibn Wahb. He said: Bakr bin Mudar informed me, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abi Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Abyssinians entered the mosque playing, and he said to me: “ Oh Humayra, do you like to look at them?” I said: “Yes.” He stood at the door, and I went to him and put my chin on his shoulder, so I supported him. With my face to his cheek, she said: And among their words at that time: Abu al-Qasim was good. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is sufficient for you,” so I said “O Messenger of God, do not be hasty.” He stood up for me and said, “It is enough for you.” I said, “Do not be hasty, O Messenger of God.” She said, “And I do not like to look at them.” But I would like women to attain his position for me, and my position with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8629","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, Aisha said, “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, covering me with his cloak, and I was looking at the Abyssinians, and they were playing.” “And I am a slave girl in the mosque, so estimate the amount of the young slave girl.”"
"8630","Amr bin Mansour told me, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told me, he said: Shuaib told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, Aisha said: By God, I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing at the door of my room, and the Abyssinians playing with spears in the mosque. He covers me with his cloak so that I can see their play, then he rises for me, so that I may be the one who hopes, so be as worthy as a modern maid. “A Sunnah keen on amusement.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8631","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: we heard it from Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: Aisha said: “It was The Abyssinians were playing with their spears, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, and I looked between his ears and his shoulders, until I was the one who \I exported\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8632","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Abyssinia played So I came behind him, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to lower his back so that I could see.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8633","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj ibn Asim, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, on the authority of Amr ibn Harith He said: “There were negroes playing in the city, so Aisha placed her chin on the shoulder of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and began to look.” \to them\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8634","Abdullah bin Muhammad al-Da'eef told me, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told me, he said: Kharijah bin Abdullah told me, he said: I am Yazid bin Roman, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sitting, and we heard commotion and the voice of children, so the Messenger of God stood up. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw an Ethiopian woman getting married and the boys around her. He said: “O Aisha, come and see.” So I came. So I placed my chin on the shoulder of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and looked at it from between the shoulder to his head, and he said to me: “As for Are you satisfied? So I started saying: No, to see my status with him, when Omar appeared, and the people refused to do so, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am looking at the devils of the jinn and mankind, who have fled from Umar.” She said: So I returned. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8635","Muhammad bin Khalaf Al-Asqalani told us, he said: We are Adam, and he is Ibn Abi Iyas, he said: We are Israel, on the authority of Qardha, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out while the Abyssinians were playing, and I was coming out of my grove, and the Messenger of God approached me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so I put my hands on his shoulders and started to look, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take the daughters of Arfidah.” And they continued playing and playing, until I was the one who finished. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8636","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu A virgin, he entered her during the days of Mina, and there were two maidservants singing and playing tambourines, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was lying on the He faced the garment, neither commanding them nor forbidding them. So Abu Bakr rebuked them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are the days of Eid.”"
"8637","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Makki bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Ja’id told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusayfa, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “O Aisha, do you know this?” She said: No, O Prophet. God said: “This is the slave girl of the son of so-and-so. Would you like her to make you sing?” So she made her sing. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8638","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He was asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the best of women, said: “The one who obeys when he commands, is pleased when he looks, and protects him with herself and his money.”"
"8639","Shuaib bin Shuaib told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: Shuaib told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Yahya told me, Bashir bin Yasar told him that Abdullah bin Muhsin told him, on the authority of a paternal aunt of his, that she had visited the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood up to fulfill some need and fulfilled her need. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to her: “ Are you a husband? She said: Yes. He said: How are you his? She said: What is wrong with him? Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Look where you are from it, for it is your Paradise and your Hell.”"
"8640","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, on the authority of his paternal aunt, She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a need. When he finished her need, he said: “Are you a husband?” She said: Yes. He said: “So how are you for him?” She said: “I only dedicate to him what I am unable to do.” He said: “Look where you are with him, for he is your heaven and your hell.” Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, He said: My aunt told me that she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something like that. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ya’la told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, that his paternal aunt, She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed, meaning Al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who is Al-Ansari. On the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, that a paternal aunt of his came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something similar. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, that Bashir bin Yasar told him, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, that his paternal aunt came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the like. Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, On the authority of Husayn ibn Muhsin who told him that a paternal aunt of his came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8641","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Husayn bin Muhsin, who said: My aunt told me that she entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, to ask him about something. He said: “Are you a husband?” She said: Yes. He said: “So how are you to him?” She said: O Messenger. God, there is no deity, said: “So do me good, for he is your Paradise and your Hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8642","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a woman spends the night seeking her husband’s bed, the angels curse her until she returns.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8643","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Mulazim bin Amr, he said: Abdullah bin Badr told me, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq bin Ali, he said: I heard the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “When a man calls his wife for his need, let her come to him, even if she is on the stove.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8644","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Bahz bin Hakim told us, he said: my father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of God Our private parts - what of them do we cover and what do we leave behind? He said: “Guard your private parts, except from your wife, or whom your right hand possesses.” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, if people are among each other in Some? He said: “If you are able to prevent anyone from seeing your private parts, then do so.” I said: What if one of us is free? He said: “By God, he is more deserving of being shy than people.”"
"8645","Hilal bin Bishr told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was told: The Jews say: If a man comes to his wife with a corpse, the child will come cross-eyed, so he said: “The Jews lied,” so it was revealed: Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage wherever you wish. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8646","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, that he used to say: “The Jews used to say: If a woman had intercourse from her anus, then She became pregnant, and her child was cross-eyed, so this verse was revealed: Your women are a field for you, so come to your field as you wish Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told me, and another mentioned, that Ibn al-Hadi He told them, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, and something similar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8647","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, who is Ibn Abdullah, he said: “The Jews were It says about a man having intercourse with his wife from the anus to her vagina: The child will be cross-eyed. So it was revealed: Your women are your tillage, so come. Your tillage wherever you wish"
"8648","Ali ibn Ma'bad informed us, he said: We were Yunus ibn Muhammad, he said: We were Ya'qub, he said: We were Ja'far, meaning Ibn Abi al-Mughirah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I have perished. He said: “ “And what destroyed you?” He said: “I moved around tonight, but nothing was answered, so this was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The verse: Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage however you wish. He says: “Come forward, and go back, and beware of the anus and the menstrual period.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8649","Ali bin Uthman bin Muhammad bin Saeed bin Abdullah bin Nufayl told us, he said: Saeed bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Tell me. Abdullah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ka’b bin Alqamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Nadr, that he told him, that he said to Nafi’, the servant of Abdullah bin Omar: You may say more than you say, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he issued a fatwa that women should be given access to their private parts. Nafi’ said: They lied to me. But I will tell you how the matter was: Ibn Omar showed the Qur’an one day, while I was with him, until your women reached a field of yours, so they came Plow with you however you wish. He said: O Nafi’, “Do you know what this verse is about? Indeed, we were a group of Quraysh who used to visit women, so when we entered Medina, and we married the women of the Ansar, we wanted from them what we wanted from our women, but behold, they disliked that and esteemed it. The women of the Ansar were only shown on their sides, so God Almighty revealed: Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage wherever you wish. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8650","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Asbagh bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: I told Malik: We have him in Egypt. Al-Layth bin Saad narrated, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yaqoub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yasar, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: We buy female slaves, and we To them, he said: “And what is the practice of acidification?” He said: “We bring them to their backs.” He said: “Or! Or does a Muslim do this?!” Then Malik said to me: I testify that Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yassar, that he asked Ibn Umar about him, and he said: “There is no problem with him.”"
"8651","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar Al-Mawsili told us, he said: Ma’an, he said: Kharijah bin Abdullah bin Sulayman bin Zayd bin told me. Thabit, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, that Ibn Omar did not see anything wrong with a man having intercourse with his wife. In her anus, Ma'n said: And I heard Malik say: I did not know that it was forbidden. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8652","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told us, he said: Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Umar, that a man had intercourse with his wife anally during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he found This was very serious, so God Almighty revealed: “Your women are your tillage, so come to your tillage however you wish.” Hisham bin Saad disagreed with him, so he narrated it. On the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8653","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdullah bin Usama bin Al-Had told me, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of the truth, so do not approach women in their behinds.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8654","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Harmi bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit, that He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of the truth.” He said it three times: “Do not approach women while they are deficient.”"
"8655","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`d ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa`d told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Yazid told me, that Ubayd Allah ibn al-Husayn He narrated to him, that Harmi bin Abdullah narrated to him, that Khuzaymah bin Thabit narrated to him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God does not “Ashamed of the truth, do not approach women in their backs.”"
"8656","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us, he said: Abdul-Malik bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Musab Abdul-Salam bin Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Al-Husayn Al-Waili, on the authority of Harami bin Abdullah Al-Waqifi, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit, He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “God is not ashamed of the truth.” He said it three times: “Do not approach women in their behinds.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: It was narrated by Al-Walid bin Kathir, and he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8657","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Abu Usama told me, he said: Al-Walid bin Kathir told me, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Al-Husayn told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Amr bin Qais Al-Khattimi, on the authority of Harami bin Abdullah, said: I heard Khuzaymah bin Thabit, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not approach women while they are naked.”"
"8658","Amr bin Hisham told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Husayn, he said: Tell me A man from my people, called: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr ibn Qays, who said: Harmi ibn Abdullah told me, he said: I was sitting in the Banu Club. Khutama, and Khuzaymah bin Thabit in the council, and he said: So they mentioned women, and what is done to them, and Khuzaymah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “O people, God is not ashamed of the truth, so do not approach women in their genitals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8659","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: I am Ishaq bin Ibrahim, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Harami bin Abdullah, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade the A woman from before her anus.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8660","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, told me that Sa`id bin Abi Hilal He narrated to him, that Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Sa’ib, one of the Banu Al-Muttalib, narrated to him, that Husayn bin Muhsin Al-Khutmi narrated to him, that Harami bin Amr Al-Khattimi told him that Khuzaymah bin Thabit told him that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of “Truly, do not approach women in their backs.”"
"8661","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri informed us, on the authority of his father, who said: We are Haywa, and he mentioned another, who said: I am Hassan, the client of Muhammad ibn Sahl, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali, on the authority of Harami bin Amr Al-Khutimi, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of the truth. Do not approach women in their backs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8662","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, he said: We are Khaled, and he is Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ali, on the authority of Harami bin Abdullah bin Ali, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “Indeed, God is not ashamed of the truth, so do not approach women in their backs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8663","Ibrahim bin Abdul Aziz bin Marwan bin Shujaa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ayan told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ali told us. Al-Shafi’i said that Abdullah bin Ali bin Al-Sa’ib told him that he heard Amr bin Uhayha bin Al-Jalah say: I heard Khuzaymah bin Thabit, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God forbids you from having sexual intercourse with women.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8664","Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi told us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, meaning Abu Ishaq al-Shafi’i, said: I heard from my grandfather through my mother. Muhammad bin Ali, he said: Abdullah bin Ali told me that he met Amr bin Uhayha bin Al-Jalah, and he asked him: Did you hear about a meeting? Does the woman have anything in her anus? He said: I bear witness that I heard Khuzaymah bin Thabit saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God forbids you from having sexual intercourse with women.” \their backs\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8665","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ali bin Al-Shafi’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, he said: Abdul told me By God, on the authority of Amr bin Uhayha Al-Ansari, he said to him: Inform me, may God grant you pleasure, about a woman having intercourse in her anus. Do you have any of it? News? He said: Yes, I bear witness that I heard Khuzaymah bin Thabit say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God forbids you from having sexual intercourse with women.” In their backs,” abbreviated (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8666","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad al-Araj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Khuzaymah Ibn Thabit, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Intercourse with women inside their backs is forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8667","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Zaida bin Abi Al-Raqqad Al-Sayrafi told us, On the authority of Amer Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the man. He had intercourse with his wife in her anus, and he said: “That is the least sodomy.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Zaida, I don’t know who she is? It is unknown, and I found it in another place: Asim Al-Ahwal"
"8668","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “It is the minor homosexuality.” Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, similarly (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8669","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Humaid al-Araj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abd Allah Ibn Amr said: “Having sexual intercourse with women in their backs is minor homosexuality.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8670","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, he said: Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulayman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a man or a woman anally.”"
"8671","Hannad bin Al-Sari told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulayman, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ On the Day of Resurrection, God will not look at a man who has intercourse with an animal or a woman in its anus.”"
"8672","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: We are Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam, he said: I am Bakr bin Mudar, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, On the authority of Uthman ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, that a man asked him about a woman having intercourse in her anus, and Muhammad said: Abdullah bin Abbas used to say: “Irrigate your field from where it grows.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8673","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abu Usama told me, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak told me, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man having intercourse with a woman in her anus. He said: “That is blasphemy.”"
"8674","Sa`id bin Ya`qub al-Talqani told us, he said: Uthman bin al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Zum`ah bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not have intercourse with women in their backs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8675","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Yazid bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Zum’ah bin Salih, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Haad said: Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be ashamed of God, for God is not ashamed of the truth, no “You come to women in their backs.”"
"8676","Othman bin Abdullah told me, he said: Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman told me, from his book, he said: Abdul Malik bin Muhammad al-San’ani told me, he said: Saeed bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Be shy From God is the right of modesty, do not approach women in their anuses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8677","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Had, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a woman in her anus.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8678","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yazid, who is the son of Abdullah bin Usama bin Al Hadd, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of Al Harith bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “God does not look at a man who has intercourse with a woman in her anus.”"
"8679","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Suhail told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God does not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8680","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On the Day of Resurrection, God will not look at a man who has intercourse with his wife in her anus.”"
"8681","Hanad bin Al-Sari and Muhammad bin Ismail bin Samurah told us, and the wording is his, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of Al-Harith ibn Mukhlid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cursed is he who has intercourse with his wife in \Put it back\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8682","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hakim al-Athram, on the authority of Abu Tamimah al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has intercourse with a menstruating woman, or with an anus woman, has disbelieved.”"
"8683","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya, Abd al-Rahman, and Bahz bin Asad told us, they said: Hammad bin Salama told us, on the authority of Hakim al-Athram On the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hujaimi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever has intercourse with a menstruating woman, or a woman in Whoever planned it, or was a soothsayer, has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8684","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “ Having intercourse with women and men behind their backs is blasphemy.”"
"8685","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “Etiyan “Men, women in their backs are disbelief.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8686","Muhammad bin Bashar told us again, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in He who has intercourse with his wife in her anus said: “That is disbelief.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8687","Muawiyah ibn Salih al-Dimashqi told me, he said: We are Mansour, meaning Ibn Abi Muzahim, he said: We are Abu Sa`id, meaning the discipliner, on the authority of Ali ibn Badhimah, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “Whoever has intercourse with the backs of men and women has committed disbelief.”"
"8688","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Waki’, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Muslim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: A Bedouin came and said: Oh Messenger of God, we are in the desert, and one of us catches a smell, and he said: “God is not ashamed of the truth, if one of you does wrong. Let him perform ablution, and do not approach women while they are naked.”"
"8689","Safwan bin Amr Al-Homsi told us, he said: Ahmed bin Khaled told us, he said: Abu Salam Abdul Malik bin Muslim bin Salam told us, on the authority of Issa bin Hattan, on the authority of Muslim bin Salam, on the authority of Ali bin Talq, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: We will be like this. The desert, and one of us smells bad, but there is little water. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you commits ablution, let him perform ablution.” “And do not approach women in their backs, for God is not ashamed of the truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8690","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Issa bin Hattan, on the authority of Muslim bin Salam, on the authority of Ali bin Talq He said: A Bedouin said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: A man from among us will be on a deserted land, and there will be a scent from him, and there will be little in the water. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you commits adultery, let him perform ablution, and do not go to women in their genitals, for God is not ashamed of \the truth\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8691","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, and Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Issa bin Hattan, on the authority of Muslim bin Salam, on the authority of Ali bin Talq, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you commits immorality, let him perform ablution, and do not go to women in their backs, for God He is not ashamed of the truth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8692","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Amer told us, he said: Ali told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Zayd bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Salam, he said: he said Abu Dharr, he said: As if the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, meant: “Indeed, every soul, every day on which the sun rises, is a charity on its part for itself.” I said: O Messenger of God, where do I get charity from, when we have no money? He said: “Isn’t it among the doors of charity: saying ‘Allahu Akbar’, ‘Praise be to God’, ‘Glory be to God’, asking God’s forgiveness, enjoining what is right, and forbidding evil?” evil, and protects the thorn from the path of Muslims, and bones and stones, and guides the blind, and guides the one who is asking to know the need of God. In her place, and strenuously raising your arms with the weak, all of that is a form of charity from you towards yourself, and you have a reward for having intercourse with your wife.” I said: How can I be rewarded for my desire? ! The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “What do you think if you had a son, and he grew up, and you hoped for his goodness, and then he died, would you expect that?” He said: Yes. He said: “So you created him?” He said: “Rather, God created him.” He said: “So you guided him?” He said: “Rather, God guided him.” He said: “So you were.” Do you provide for him?” He said: “Rather, God provided for him.” He said: “Likewise, put him in what is lawful, and keep away from what is unlawful. If God wills, He will give him life, and if He wills.” He caused him to die, and you will be rewarded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8693","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I Hisham, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abi Uyaynah, on the authority of Yahya bin Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Yamar, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A charity is given to all my descendants of the son of Adam every day,” and then he said: Removing harmful things from the road is a charity, your greeting of greetings to people is a charity, enjoining what is right is a charity, and forbidding evil is a charity. And bargaining with your family is charity.” We said: O Messenger of God, can a man satisfy his desire and give him charity? ! He said: “Yes, do you think that if he had made that desire something for which God had forbidden it, would it not have been a burden on him?” We said: Yes. He said: “Then if he made it Whatever God has made lawful for him, it is charity.” He said: He mentioned some things that are charity, then he said: “The two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer are sufficient for all of that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8694","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahim told us, he said: Amr bin Abi Salamah told us, on the authority of Sadaqa bin Abdullah, on the authority of Zuhayr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sarjis, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you goes to his family, Let him apply something to his incapacity and her incapacity, and do not disgrace them as if they were disgraced.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith. 5 And Sadaqah bin Abd Allah is weak. 5 I only included it so that Amr would not be made Zaheer (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8695","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he reports With it, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of them, when having an affair with his family, said: In the name of God, O God, spare us Satan, and protect You did not provide us with Satan, so a child was decreed between them, and Satan did not harm him.” Ibn Abi Umar disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8696","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told us, he said: Ibn Abi Omar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you, when he goes to his family, says: In the name of God, O God, spare me.” Satan, and protect Satan as long as You have provided for us. Then a child was decreed between them, and Satan did not harm him.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith."
"8697","Ibrahim bin Muhammad al-Taymi, the judge of Basra, told us, he said: Ibn Dawud told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Suleiman bin Dawud, peace be upon them, said: I will go around a hundred women tonight. Then each woman brought a man who would strike with a sword, and he did not say: God willing. So he went around them, and one woman brought half a child, even if he had said Suleiman: God willing, what he said would have happened. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8698","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Anas bin Malik told us, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, “he used to go about his wives at every hour of the day and night, and there were eleven of them.” I said to Anas: Could he tolerate that? He said: We were talking about “being given the strength of thirty.”"
"8699","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, that some people told them, that the Prophet God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to go around his wives in one night, and on that day he had nine wives.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8700","Muhammad ibn Muammar informed us, he said: I am Habban, he said: I am Hammad ibn Salamah, he said: I am Abd al-Rahman ibn Fulan ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his paternal aunt. Salma, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went around his wives one day, and he began to bathe at this time, and when This, I said: O Messenger of God, if you made it one wash, he said: “This is purer, more pleasant, and more pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8701","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to “circulate around his wives in one bath.”"
"8702","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He goes around his wives in one night, then he takes a bath once.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: The correct hadith is the hadith of Qatada. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8703","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he narrated the hadith, he said “If one of you visits his family and then wants to return, let him perform ablution.”"
"8704","Harun bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Hafs, who is Ibn Ghayath, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever visits his family at the beginning of the night, then wants to return at the end of the night, let him perform ablution in between.” “Ablution”"
"8705","Abdul Malik bin Abdul Hamid told us, he said: Abu Omar Al-Hudhi told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Asim Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, On the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said about the one who touches his wife and then wants to go back. He said: “He should perform ablution before he goes back.” \. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake"," but the correct thing is the hadith of Ibn al-Mubarak and Hafs bin Ghayath. (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8706","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us. H Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, he said: My father told me, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, on the authority of Urwa On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to sleep while he was in a state of junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8707","Safwan bin Amr told me, on the authority of Ali bin Ayyash, he said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to sleep while in a state of junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer.”"
"8708","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, said, “If he comes to his family and wants to lie down, he should perform his ablution for prayer.” Al-Nasa’i said: The correct hadith is the hadith of Ishaq, and the hadith of Ali bin Ayyash is wrong."
"8709","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading it, and I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Al-Layth, and Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to sleep while he was in a state of junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer.” \before he sleeps\"""""
"8710","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that Aisha, she said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “If he wanted to sleep while in a state of junubah, he would perform his ablution for prayer, and if he wanted to eat, Or he drinks,” she said: “He washes his hands, then he eats and drinks.”"
"8711","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki`, he said: Saleh told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “If he wants to eat while he is in a state of ritual impurity, he should wash his hands.”"
"8712","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid, who is the son of Zurayi, said: Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to sleep, or eat while he was in a state of sexual intercourse, he would perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8713","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: we, then Sufyan mentioned after him, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “if he wanted to sleep while he was in a state of junub, he would perform his ablution for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8714","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If he is in a state of impurity and wants to sleep, he should perform his ablution for prayer.”"
"8715","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: “He sleeps while he is in his state of state, and does not touch water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8716","Ismail bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Musa bin Ayan told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to relieve himself, then sleep, then pour water over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8717","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Hushaym told me, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to sleep while he was in a state of state.”"
"8718","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: We are Qarad, and he is Abdul-Rahman bin Ghazwan Abu Nuh, he said: I am Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, that he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: When does one of us sleep while he is junub? He said: “Wash your penis, then perform ablution and go to sleep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8719","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said, “He was in a state of ritual impurity during the night, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: ‘Perform ablution, wash your penis, then sleep.’”"
"8720","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Salih bin Qudamah, he said: Ibn Dinar told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar mentioned to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was afflicted with ritual impurity during the night, so he said: “Let him perform ablution, wash his penis, and sleep.”"
"8721","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ubaidah, and others, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was asked: Can a man lie down while he is junub? He said: “Yes, if he performs ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8722","Sahl bin Salih told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: I said: O Messenger By God, can one of us sleep while he is in a state of jannah? He said: “He performs ablution.”"
"8723","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah and he is Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar said: O Messenger of God, does one of us lie down while he is in a state of junubah? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you wants to do that, let him perform ablution.”"
"8724","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, he told him, that Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Will one of us lie down while junub? He said: “Yes, if he performs ablution.”"
"8725","Humayd ibn Masada told us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar was afflicted with a ritual impurity. So Omar came and mentioned that to him, so Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him for advice, and he said: “Perform ablution and lie down.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8726","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Mu’alla told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Omar, and Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When does one of us sleep while he is in a state of junub? In the hadith of Nafi’, he said: “Let him perform ablution, then let him sleep,” and in the hadith of Abu Qilaba: “Let him perform his ablution for prayer, then let him sleep.”"
"8727","Imran bin Yazid bin Abi Humaid Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Ismail bin Abdullah told me, he said: I am Al-Awza’i, he said: Osama told me Ibn Zaid, he said: Nafi’ told me, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told me, that Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When does one of us sleep? And he is on the side? So he ordered him to “wash his private parts and perform ablution.”"
"8728","Shuaib bin Shuaib bin Ishaq Al-Dimashqi told me, he said: Abdul Wahhab bin Saeed told me, he said: Shuaib bin Ishaq told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i He said: Amr bin Saad told me, he said: Nafi’ told me, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told me, he said: Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said: How can one of us sleep while he is in a state of junub? He said: “Yes, and he should perform ablution.”"
"8729","Muhammad bin Musfa bin Bahloul Al-Humsi told us, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya told me, he said: Nafi’ told me, On the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When does one of us sleep while he is junub? He said: “Yes, he performs ablution and goes to sleep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8730","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abu Al-Mughirah, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, Omar, asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: How long does one of us sleep while he is in a state of junub? He said: “Yes, and he should perform ablution.”"
"8731","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Harrani informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir told us, on the authority of al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he asked him: When does one of us sleep while he is in a state of junub? He said: “Yes, and let him perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8732","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told me, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Omar, he said: O Messenger of God, when does one of us sleep while he is in a state of junub? He said: “Yes, and he should perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8733","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that “if he wanted to eat, sleep, or drink, he would perform his ablution for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8734","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad informed us, he said: Shu`bah informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Ibn Umar, That “if he wanted to eat, sleep, or drink while he was in a state of ritual impurity, he would perform his ablution for prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8735","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ali, who said: “If a man becomes junub and wants to If he sleeps or eats food, let him perform his ablution for prayer.”"
"8736","Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Sufi told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Abdullah Ibn al-Walid told us, and he used to sit with Al-Hasan bin Hayy, on the authority of Bukair bin Shihab, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Jews came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Abu Al-Qasim, we ask you about some things, and if you answer us about them, we will follow you, believe you, and believe in you. He said: So he took from them what he took. Israel is upon its children, when they said: God is the disposer of what we say. They said: Tell us about the sign of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “You sleep.” His eyes, and his heart does not sleep.” They said: “And tell us how a woman becomes feminine, and how a man becomes male?” He said: “The two waters meet, so if the woman’s water comes over the man’s water, she becomes female, and if the man’s water comes over the woman’s water, she males.” They said: You are right. They said: So tell us about thunder, what is it? He said: “An angel from among the angels, entrusted with the clouds. He has holes of fire with which he drives the clouds wherever God wills.” They said: What is this sound that Is he heard? He said: “He will repel him with the clouds when he rebukes them, until he ends up where he is commanded.” They said: You are right. They said: Tell us what Israel has forbidden to itself? He said: “He lived with Bedouins, and he complained of sciatica, and he did not find anything to blame except camel meat and milk, so he forbade them.” They said: You have spoken the truth. They said: Tell us who of the angels comes to you, for there is no prophet except that an angel of the angels comes to him from Lord with the message and with the revelation, who is your companion? For this only remains, until we follow you. He said: “It is Gabriel.” They said: He is the one who sends down war and killing. Our enemy is among the angels. If you said: Michael, who sends down rain and mercy, we would follow you. Then God Almighty revealed: Whoever is an enemy. To Gabriel, until the end of the verse: Indeed, God is an enemy to the unbelievers. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8737","Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, on the authority of Marwan bin Muhammad, he said: Muawiyah bin Salam told me, he said: My brother told me, that he heard his grandfather Abu Salam He says: Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told me, on the authority of Thawban, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a rabbi from The rabbis of the Jews, and he said: Peace be upon you, Muhammad. He said: So I pushed him until I knocked him down, and he said: Why did you push me? I said: Don't you say, O Messenger of God? Then the Jew said: I call him by the name by which his family called him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Yes, my family called me Muhammad.” He said: I came to ask. He said: “Would it benefit you if I told you?” He said: “I hear with my ears,” so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Ask whatever seems to you.” Then the Jew said: What have you seen, if the heavens were changed to other heavens and the earth to other earth, where would the people be? He said: “In the darkness below the bridge.” He said: Who is the first person to be rewarded by God? He said: “The poor immigrants.” He said: What will the people of Paradise be given as a gift? He said: “The excess of Nun’s liver.” He said: What did they eat after that? He said: “The bull of Paradise, which used to eat from its outskirts, will be slaughtered for them.” He said: What will they drink? He said: “From a spring called Salsabil.” He said: You are right. The Jew said: I ask you about one thing that only a prophet, or one or two men, knows about. He said: “Would it benefit you if I told you?” He said: “I hear with my ears.” He said: “Ask whatever seems to you.” He said: Where does the boy’s likeness come from? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man’s semen is thick and white, while a woman’s semen is yellow and thin. The woman will be masculine, God willing, and if the woman’s semen is above the man’s semen, she will become feminine, God willing. He said: You have spoken the truth, and you are a prophet. Then He went, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He asked me when he asked me, and I have no knowledge until God informed me of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8738","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Humaid, he said: Anas told us, that Abdullah bin Salam informed him The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina and came to him and asked him about some things. He said: I am asking you about three things that no one knows except a prophet: What is the first sign of the Hour? What is the first food that the people of Paradise will eat? Why is it that a child is drawn to his mother and his father? He said: “Gabriel told me about them just now.” Abdullah bin Salam said: That is a number, and the Jews are among the angels. He said: As for “the first of the signs.” The Hour: A fire will emerge from the east to the west, and the first food that the people of Paradise will eat is the excess of the liver of a whale. As for the child: So when a man’s ejaculation precedes a man’s sexual intercourse, it is removed from him, and when a woman’s ejaculation precedes it, then the likeness is removed.” He said: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that You are the Messenger of God. He said: O Messenger of God, the Jews are a confused people, so ask them about me before they learn of my Islam. Then the Jews came He said: “Which man is Abdullah bin Salam among you?” They said: The best of us, the son of the best of us, the best of us, and the son of the best of us. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Did you not see if Abdullah bin Salam converted to Islam?” They said: May God protect him from that, so he brought it back, so they said something like that, Then Abdullah bin Salam came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. They said: Our evil, and the son of our evil. They investigated him, and he said: This is what I feared, O Messenger of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8739","Amr bin Mansour al-Nasa’i and Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim al-Awdi told us, saying: Muhammad bin al-Salt al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Kadina Yahya bin Al-Muhallab Al-Kufi, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: A Jew passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was speaking to his companions. He said: The Quraysh said: O Jew, this He claims to be a prophet, so he said: I will ask him about something that only a prophet knows. So he came until he sat down and said: O Muhammad, what is man created from? He said: “O Jew, each is created from the sperm of the man, and from the sperm of the woman. As for the sperm of the man, it is a thick sperm, from which Bone and nerve, and as for the woman’s sperm, it is a delicate sperm, including flesh and blood.” So the Jew stood up. The pronunciation is for Ahmad. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib had changed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8740","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, that Anas bin Malik He told them that Umm Sulaym asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He said: “When she sees water, let her wash herself,” Umm Salamah said, and I felt ashamed because of that: Will that be, O Messenger of God? ! He said: “Yes, a man’s water is thick and white, and a woman’s water is thin and yellow, so whichever of them is higher, or earlier, there is a resemblance to it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8741","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us, he said: It was narrated by Abdah, he said: It was Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of his mother, Umm Sulaym, that she asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reported on the authority of a woman who sees in her dreams what a man sees. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If she sees “Woman, or one of you, let her wash.” Umm Salamah said: “Will this be the case?” ! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman’s water is thin and yellow, and a man’s water is thick and white. “similarity”"
"8742","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: It was narrated by Abd al-Ala, he said: It was Muammar, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Thuban, on the authority of Jabir Ibn Abdullah, said: We had female slaves, and we used to isolate ourselves from them, so the Jews said: That friendly woman Minor, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about that, and he said: “The Jews lied. If God had wanted to create them, they could not have \return it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8743","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Muhammad bin Hisham told me Abd al-Rahman bin Thawban said: Abu Rifa`ah told me that Abu Sa`id al-Khudri said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: I have a daughter, and I am isolated from her, and I want from her what a man wants, and the Jews claimed that the youngest Isolation, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews lied. If God had wanted to create him, you would not have been able to avert him.” Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar informed us, he said: I am Ali, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, That Abu Muti’ bin Awf, one of the Banu Rifa’ah bin Al-Harith, told him, that Abu Sa’id told him, something like that. Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Harun bin Ismail informed us, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Muti’ bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a similar hadith Othman bin Omar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8744","Yahya bin Durst al-Basri told us, he said: Abu Ismail al-Qannad told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Muhammad bin Abd The Most Gracious narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Muti’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I have a female servant. I desire what men desire, and I am isolated from her. I hate for her to become pregnant, and the Jews claim that isolation is the youngest woman. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews lied, the Jews lied. If God had wanted to create him, you would not have been able to do so.” \You spend it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"8745","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Abu Amir speaking, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It was said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The Jews say: The isolation is the smallest friend. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Jews lied. If God had intended to create them, you would not have been able to remove them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
